## Tests

`world_water_bodies_test` has 22 tests:
- the roadmap's four labelling cases: an island is one sea; a hollow is one lake; two hollows are two lakes; a channel joins a hollow to the sea;
- inlets at opposite edges are one sea;
- 8-connectivity;
- the pond / lake threshold;
- dry and flooded grids;
- a straight shore: exact distance, normal, slope and depth;
- the shore distance against brute force on a random wet/dry pattern;
- smoothing: it keeps a straight shore's normal and turns the medial-axis snap from 90° into a gentle turn;
- fetch on a rectangle, either way round;
- the water level;
- missing ground (NaN counts as dry);
- determinism;
- bad grids;
- off-grid queries;
- generated worlds: the water sits on the mesh's samples; an island world is ringed by sea; the stride keeps large worlds to 1025;
- the Water bodies colour mode, on the ground's texture and on the water's.

`ariadne_scene_world_test` now also checks that the headless host publishes `world.stats.water`.

`algo_distance_transform_test` has 5 tests:
- distances against brute force;
